      "description": "Watch Abha vs Al Khaleej Saihat highlights and goals from Pro League - Saudi Arabia on ReFooty: Football Highlights Hub. Match played on August 25, 2026. On August 25, 2026, Abha and Al Khaleej Saihat faced off in a crucial Pro League encounter that promised to test the tactical mettle of both squads. With both teams eager to climb the table, the stage was set for a match defined by high energy and clinical execution. Early Fireworks and Dominance The home side wasted no time establishing their authority on the pitch, catching the visitors cold with a relentless attacking rhythm. The breakthrough came in the 17th minute when Joshua King showcased his finishing prowess, slotting home to give Abha the early advantage. The momentum remained firmly with the hosts, and just seven minutes later, in the 24th minute, Keshim Al-Qahtani doubled the lead. The goal was beautifully crafted, following a precise assist from Mohammed Al-Dawsari that carved open the Al Khaleej defense, leaving the visitors with a mountain to climb before the break. Tactical Shifts and Midfield Battle In a bid to turn the tide, Al Khaleej introduced a triple substitution at the start of the second half, bringing on Nabil Fekir , Alimami Gory , and Saleh Al-Amri . These changes injected fresh life into their play, forcing Abha into a more defensive posture. The contest grew increasingly physical as the minutes ticked by, with the referee busy issuing cautions. Michy Batshuayi saw yellow for Abha in the 51st minute, followed ten minutes later by Pedro Rebocho for the visitors, as the battle for control in the center of the park intensified. Late Drama and Final Whistle As the match entered its closing stages, a flurry of substitutions from both managers aimed to manage fatigue and preserve the scoreline. Abha 's defensive unit stood tall against late pressure, successfully neutralizing the threats posed by the refreshed Al Khaleej attack. In the 91st minute, Mustafa Malayekah received a yellow card as tensions flared during stoppage time. However, the result was never truly in doubt, and when the final whistle blew after five minutes of added time, Abha celebrated a well-earned victory built on their clinical first-half display."
